From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:23:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give sent documents a file name

send_file_document() puts the document's name only into Title.
Receivers name a document after FileName, so every document sent from
here arrived without a name: this plug-in on the other side saved it
under its content hash (for example <sha256>.zip), the transfer had no
name to show, and the original name was gone.

Set FileName as well. When receiving, fall back to Title if FileName
is empty, so documents from senders that set only the title still get
their name.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/hoehermann/purple-gowhatsapp/pull/310]
---
 handle_attachment.go | 4 ++++
 send_file.go         | 1 +
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/handle_attachment.go b/handle_attachment.go
index 062de4f..5763b75 100644
--- a/handle_attachment.go
+++ b/handle_attachment.go
@@ -153,6 +153,10 @@ func (handler *Handler) handle_attachment(message *waE2E.Message, id string, sou
 			downloadable = dm
 			hash = hex.EncodeToString(dm.GetFileSHA256())
 			filename = dm.GetFileName()
+			if filename == "" {
+				// documents sent by older versions of this plug-in carry their name only as the title
+				filename = dm.GetTitle()
+			}
 			extension = filepath.Ext(filename)
 			if extension != "" {
 				// remove extension from filename for consistency when using file-naming template
diff --git a/send_file.go b/send_file.go
index 76df4be..4bdd177 100644
--- a/send_file.go
+++ b/send_file.go
@@ -189,6 +189,7 @@ func (handler *Handler) send_file_document(data []byte, mimetype string, filenam
 	}
 	msg := &waE2E.Message{DocumentMessage: &waE2E.DocumentMessage{
 		Title:         proto.String(filename),
+		FileName:      proto.String(filename),
 		URL:           proto.String(uploaded.URL),
 		DirectPath:    proto.String(uploaded.DirectPath),
 		MediaKey:      uploaded.MediaKey,
